# GATE-EXEMPT: the project's ruling on which paths need no gate rows (copy to .team/gate-exempt)
#
# Read by scripts/gate-check-range AT THE PUSHED TIP (like the ledger), by the local push
# hook and by the server workflow alike, so there is one rule set. One entry per line.
# This file is a RULING, not a convenience: name the decision that set it in a # line, and
# change it only with a new decision.
#
#   exempt <path>   every changed path matching it makes the commit exempt
#   keep <path>     a path under an exempt entry that is NOT exempt (for example docs the
#                   deploy ships into the running product)
#   never <path>    a path that is never exempt whatever else matches
#
# A commit is exempt only when EVERY changed path matches an exempt entry and NONE matches
# a keep or never entry. A commit that mixes an exempt path with anything else is checked.
# A rename out of code into an exempt directory shows both paths and is checked.
# Path forms: "docs/" is the directory and everything under it; an entry with * ? or [ is
# a shell glob against the whole repo-relative path ("*.md" is every Markdown file at any
# depth); anything else is an exact file or a directory of that name.
# Absent or empty: only the built-in exemptions apply (.team-only and tree-identical).
#
# Decision: <D-nn, date, who ruled>
#
# EXAMPLE (uncomment and edit; this set exempts documentation but keeps shipped docs gated):
# exempt docs/
# exempt discussion/
# exempt README.md
# keep docs/guide/help-content-seed.md
# keep docs/eligibility-documents/
# never tools/
# never .github/
# never src/
